{
  "_comment": [
    "Declarations for the Lodestone census (tools/lodestone_census.py).",
    "",
    "The census enumerates every field in fable2_settings.h itself. This file",
    "does not list subjects - it explains the ones the census cannot verify on",
    "its own, and every entry needs a reason a person can disagree with.",
    "",
    "'reason' declares a setting that is deliberately not in the settings UI.",
    "'doc_phrase' gives the words the README's settings reference uses for it,",
    "because that reference is written for players and says 'Detail strength',",
    "not 'texture_ai_strength'. Without it the census would demand identifiers",
    "in prose, which would make the docs worse to pass a test.",
    "'undocumented_ok' declares a setting that is reachable but is not worth a",
    "line in the README - internal state a player sets by using the app.",
    "'guarded_by' names another setting that decides whether this one is sent",
    "to the plugin at all, when that is the design: a sharpness only means",
    "something while its filter is the chosen one."
  ],
  "declared": [
    {
      "setting": "hardware_detected",
      "reason": "a run-once latch, not a knob. It records that first-run hardware detection has happened so a value the player edited afterwards is never overwritten by a later launch.",
      "undocumented_ok": true
    },
